expo-01.answer:
To keep the splash screen visible while loading resources or API data, use `preventAutoHideAsync()` to manually control when it hides [3]. 

Here is an example using Expo Router [3]:

```tsx app/_layout.tsx
import { Stack } from 'expo-router';
import * as SplashScreen from 'expo-splash-screen';
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

// Keep the splash screen visible while we fetch resources
SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync();

export default function RootLayout() {
  const [isReady, setIsReady] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    async function doAsyncStuff() {
      try {
        // do something async here
      } catch (e) {
        console.warn(e);
      } finally {
        setIsReady(true);
      }
    }

    doAsyncStuff();
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (isReady) {
      SplashScreen.hide();
    }
  }, [isReady]);

  if (!isReady) {
    return null;
  }

  return <Stack />;
}
```

expo-05.answer:
To protect screens so only signed-in users can access them, you can use `Stack.Protected` (or `Tabs.Protected`) with a `guard` prop based on your authentication state [2].

Here is an example setup in your root layout (`src/app/_layout.tsx`):

```tsx src/app/_layout.tsx
import { Stack } from 'expo-router';
import { useAuthState } from '@/utils/authState';

export default function RootLayout() {
  const { isLoggedIn } = useAuthState();

  return (
    <Stack>
      <Stack.Protected guard={isLoggedIn}>
        <Stack.Screen name="(tabs)" />
        <Stack.Screen name="modal" />
      </Stack.Protected>

      <Stack.Protected guard={!isLoggedIn}>
        <Stack.Screen name="sign-in" />
        <Stack.Screen name="create-account" />
      </Stack.Protected>
    </Stack>
  );
}
```

### Key behaviors:
* **Automatic redirection:** "If you wrap this screen in a `Stack.Protected` with the `guard={false}`, the screen will become inaccessible and the next available screen will be opened instead." [2]
* **Deep link protection:** "Protected routes are checked even if you deep link into a page directly. For example, if an unauthenticated user deep links into the modal screen above, they will be redirected to the sign-in page." [2]

