To configure background location on iOS with `expo-location`, you need to add the `location` value to the `UIBackgroundModes` array [6]. 

If you are using Continuous Native Generation (CNG), the required `UIBackgroundModes` configuration is applied automatically by prebuild when you set `"isIosBackgroundLocationEnabled": true` in your app config [4][6]:

```json app.json
{
  "expo": {
    "plugins": [
      [
        "expo-location",
        {
          "isIosBackgroundLocationEnabled": true
        }
      ]
    ]
  }
}
```

If you are not using CNG or are configuring a native iOS project manually, add the following to your **Expo.plist** file [6]:

```xml ios/project-name/Supporting/Expo.plist
<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
  <array>
    <string>location</string>
  </array>
```

