You can check if the app is running on iOS or Android by using `Platform.OS` from the `react-native` module [4]. 

`Platform.OS` will be `"ios"` when running on iOS and `"android"` when running on Android [4].

```tsx
import {Platform, StyleSheet} from 'react-native';

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  height: Platform.OS === 'ios'? 200: 100,
});
```

You can also use `Platform.select` to return platform-specific values or components [4]:

```tsx
import {Platform, StyleSheet} from 'react-native';

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
...Platform.select({
      ios: {
        backgroundColor: 'red',
      },
      android: {
        backgroundColor: 'green',
      },
      default: {
        // other platforms, web for example
