To react to every change as the user types into a `TextInput`, you can use the `onChangeText` or `onChange` props.

* `onChangeText`: "Callback that is called when the text input's text changes. Changed text is passed as a single string argument to the callback handler." [1]
* `onChange`: "Callback that is called when the text input's text changes." [1]

Here is a minimal example using `onChangeText`:

```tsx
import {useState} from 'react';
import {StyleSheet, TextInput} from 'react-native';
import {SafeAreaView, SafeAreaProvider} from 'react-native-safe-area-context';

const TextInputExample = () => {
  const [text, onChangeText] = useState('Useless Text');

  return (
    <SafeAreaProvider>
      <SafeAreaView>
        <TextInput
          style={styles.input}
          onChangeText={onChangeText}
          value={text}
        />
      </SafeAreaView>
    </SafeAreaProvider>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  input: {
    height: 40,
    margin: 12,
    borderWidth: 1,
    padding: 10,
  },
});

export default TextInputExample;
```

